==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|loup|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*laubą}}, perhaps from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*leup-||peel, break off}}. Compare Low German {{term|Loov|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|loof|lang=nl}}, English {{term|leaf|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|løv|lang=da}}.

